/api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Adds an external consumer that binds a narrow artifact-identity authorization to an independently supplied scenario contract, authenticated review, scenario-dependent checker independence and explicit consumed claim scope. Existing RVR receipt bytes, Core sources and historical v0-v4 evidence are preserved.\n\nThis Draft PR is stacked on #4 (ee1143f2b8f669a88f36c736d20bb86c2ade950a). It does not change #2/#3/#4 or main. No upstream PR or merge is requested.\n\nValidation: 45 scenarios, 17 tests in normal/repeat/Python -O; corrected mutation inventory: 16 killed, 1 survived, no crashes. The surviving contract-preimage fallback still refuses when both carriers are absent; this boundary is not certified as isolated mutation coverage. The initial 17-kill witness retained a second preimage carrier; its evidence is preserved and superseded explicitly. Semantic outputs are deterministic. Historical v0-v4 suites and original mutation classifications were reproduced. Frozen Core: 13 vendored files and all 75 tracked upstream files unchanged. Genuine laboratory EIP-712 signatures are checked by Node and eth-account; RVR Python/TypeScript gates replay independently.\n\nSee research/erc8404/EXPERIMENT_RESULTS.md for comparative counts and raw evidence. A/B results measure intentionally incomplete downstream lifts, not defects in ERC-8404. Contract adequacy remains external. No external execution, judgment truth, full real chain, scientific novelty or general security claim is made.\n\nRecommendation: COMPATIBLE_WITH_FROZEN_CORE for this external consumer route. A new normative Verification Profile and deployed ERC-8274/WYRIWE/8412 integration are not claimed.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_